WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.420
When it comes to dating, loving your
enemy is not so easy. A new American

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.150
Perspective Survey by AEI finds that
politics is creeping into our love lives.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.000
62% of Americans say it would be
impossible to date someone whose views

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.600
of the president did not align with
their own. But not all Americans are

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.609
equally likely to say Trump is a factor
in their dating decisions. Almost 80% of

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.119
Democratic women say they would be
unwilling to date someone whose view of

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:36.000
Trump contrasted with their own. But for
Republican men, Trump is much less of an issue.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.540
It's not surprising that Trump has
intruded into our dating lives. Through

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.170
social media and non-stop news coverage,
Trump has made himself an omnipresent

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.460
feature of American public life. And
compared to past presidents, Trump

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.420
inspires very strong feelings on both
sides. Most Americans have a very

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.699
favorable or a very unfavorable opinion
of Trump, and yet few Americans believe

00:00:56.699 --> 00:01:00.329
that political differences will doom a
relationship. Most believe that

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.439
disagreements over finances and children
are more pressing concerns for couples

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:10.080
than politics. Would you date someone
who doesn't share your political views?

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.040
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.180
scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.799
research and videos from AEI.

